WEBVTT

00:04:57.916 --> 00:05:01.516
set my boyfriend's brain
to Lance Armstrong,

00:05:01.516 --> 00:05:03.116
the ugly sister.

00:05:03.156 --> 00:05:06.996
Now, he was stuck in the wrong neural
neighborhood and couldn't get out.

00:05:07.396 --> 00:05:10.876
The ugly sister also explains
this phenomenon.

00:05:10.916 --> 00:05:14.276
Much later, once you've stopped
trying to find the word,

00:05:14.276 --> 00:05:18.516
it suddenly bubbles to the surface,
seemingly out of nowhere.

00:05:18.516 --> 00:05:19.836
Laird Hamilton.

00:05:19.876 --> 00:05:21.836
Yes, that's it.

00:05:21.876 --> 00:05:23.556
Why does that happen?

00:05:24.076 --> 00:05:25.636
By calling off the hunt,

00:05:25.676 --> 00:05:29.116
your brain can stop
perseverating on the ugly sister,

00:05:29.156 --> 00:05:32.716
giving the correct set of neurons
a chance to be activated.